    {"id": "versions-agent", "since": "0.2", "area": "backend", "claim": "The Versions screen reads the host's version agent over its socket; an owner updates a component against the current revision; the agent pins binaries by catalogue hash and rolls back on a failed restart.", "proof": ["pytest::panel/tests/test_versions.py::test_version_update_requires_owner_and_current_revision", "pytest::panel/tests/test_versions.py::test_version_update_rejects_viewer", "pytest::tests/test_version_agent.py::test_binary_update_uses_catalog_hash_and_persists_revision", "pytest::tests/test_version_agent.py::test_binary_update_rolls_back_when_service_restart_fails"], "routes": ["GET /api/versions", "POST /api/versions/{component}/update"], "status": "proven"},
    {"id": "clients-and-grants", "since": "0.2", "area": "clients", "claim": "A client with access grants on every protocol: one journalled operation per request, a bundle reveal of every artifact, grant enable/disable/rotate/delete reaching the manager and audited, a client suspended or archived by state.", "proof": ["pytest::panel/tests/test_client_import.py::test_creating_several_grants_is_one_journalled_operation", "pytest::panel/tests/test_grant_lifecycle.py::test_local_grant_lifecycle_reaches_the_manager_and_is_audited", "pytest::panel/tests/test_grant_lifecycle.py::test_local_delete_purges_the_row_at_once_and_frees_the_name", "pytest::panel/tests/test_grant_lifecycle.py::test_grant_routes_map_errors_and_check_csrf", "fleet::s05", "fleet::s06", "pytest::panel/tests/test_ui_browser_findings.py::test_a_mieru_grant_without_options_means_no_quota"], "routes": ["GET /api/clients", "POST /api/clients", "GET /api/clients/{client_id}", "POST /api/clients/{client_id}/grants", "POST /api/clients/{client_id}/state", "POST /api/clients/grants/{grant_id}/{action}", "POST /api/operations/{operation_id}/bundle", "GET /api/operations/{operation_id}"], "status": "fixed-in-0.6"},
    {"id": "provisioning-saga", "since": "0.2", "area": "clients", "claim": "Idempotent manager operations with a durable journal: every injected fault ends in a declared outcome, a crashed operation resumes (through the API too), compensation never deletes what it did not create.", "proof": ["pytest::panel/tests/test_provisioning_saga.py::test_every_fault_ends_in_a_declared_outcome_and_resumes", "pytest::panel/tests/test_provisioning_saga.py::test_compensation_never_deletes_what_the_operation_did_not_create", "pytest::panel/tests/test_client_import.py::test_an_interrupted_operation_is_resumed_through_the_api"], "routes": ["POST /api/operations/{operation_id}/resume"], "status": "fixed-in-0.6"},
